ear_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_power_series_f8394d94_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"In the power series $\\sum_{n = 0}^{\\infty} 3^n(x-2)^n$, what is the second coefficient $c_2$?","options":["$9$","$2$","$3$","$6$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2171f65a2e9f1787129c7920","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_power_series_f8394d94_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which expression is a power series centred at $-2$?","options":["$\\sum_{n = 0}^{\\infty} c_n(x-2)^n$","$\\sum_{n = 0}^{\\infty} c_n(x+2)^n$","$\\sum_{n = 0}^{\\infty} c_nx^{-2n}$","$\\sum_{n = 0}^{\\infty} c_n(2-x)^n$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ba7ccb484b65239dfc8b8890","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_power_series_f8394d94_014","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What kind of object is the sequence $(c_n)_{n=0}^{\\infty}$ in a power series?","options":["A sequence of input values depending on $x$","A finite list of powers of $x$","A sequence of real coefficients independent of $x$","A sequence of centres"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"83d6d1a5332dbdeedfc880c8","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_power_series_f8394d94_015","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which term of $\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} c_n(x-a)^n$ corresponds to $n=0$?","options":["$c_0(x-a)$","$c_1(x-a)$","$0$","$c_0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"29249a906d0b8b7a3c1f3a1d","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_power_series_f8394d94_017","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"In $\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{n+1}(x+3)^n$, what is the centre?","options":["$3$","$0$","$1$","$-3$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"03c8da11f6710f782bc423ea","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_power_series_f8394d94_018","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is the coefficient $c_2$ in $1+4(x-a)+7(x-a)^2+\\cdots$?","options":["$4$","$7$","$1$","$a$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"eff87c92498ec702c0945f40","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_power_series_f8394d94_020","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which coefficient sequence gives $1+x+\\frac{x^2}{2}+\\frac{x^3}{6}+\\cdots$ as a power series centered at $0$?","options":["$c_n=n!$","$c_n=\\frac{1}{n!}$","$c_n=n$","$c_n=0$ for all $n$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0059344db0a09b96e570d4e2","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_power_series_f8394d94_009_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why does the formal expression $\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} c_n(x-a)^n$ not by itself tell you for which $x$ the power series converges?","options":["Every expression of this form converges for all real $x$.","The definition fixes only the form; whether the series converges depends on the $c_n$ and on $|x-a|$.","Every expression of this form diverges at every point $x\\neq a$ unless all of its coefficients $c_n$ are equal to zero.","A power series is only defined once its sum is known in closed form."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"1546f65affad24bcb8b1eefa","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_power_series_f8394d94_011_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Write the polynomial $2+3x$ as a power series $\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}c_nx^n$ centred at $0$. Which coefficient sequence is correct?","options":["$c_0=3$, $c_1=2$, and $c_n=0$ for all $n\\ge2$","$c_n=2+3n$ for all $n$","$c_0=0$, $c_1=2$, and $c_n=3$ for all $n\\ge2$","$c_0=2$, $c_1=3$, and $c_n=0$ for all $n\\ge2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c33d30bc193f2fcd87ce29e0","time_limit":40}]}}